From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:51:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: make the MSM8226 HFI 1xx decoder work with
 stateful clients

Stock FFmpeg's V4L2 decoder crashed the MSM8226 Venus firmware or
received two frames. Qualified on the Fx0 in RAM trials (byte-exact
12-frame and 120-frame H.264 decodes, matching timestamps):

- Start the session at the negotiated coded size, report that geometry
  at OUTPUT streamon and hold coded input until CAPTURE streams, so
  the firmware has capture buffers before it decodes a picture; ignore
  the firmware's confirming sequence event.
- Size capture buffers from the firmware requirements by default and
  keep a sufficient scratch allocation across reconfiguration instead
  of releasing it.
- Do not resend continue-data-transfer, the raw format and allocation
  mode on reconfiguration, and omit the unused secondary buffer count.
- The firmware returns no timestamps: take the earliest pending input
  timestamp for each picture and do not consume entries on input
  completion.

Debug-level tracing and default-off probes from the diagnostic branch
diagnostic/fx0-venus-r13-retain-props-01 are retained.

Assisted-by: LLM [Claude Code]
